From: Dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: correct the TLV peer 160 MHz flag

The TLV firmware interface uses bit 29 to identify a P2P-capable peer
and bit 30 for a peer operating at 160 MHz. The ath10k TLV peer flag
map currently puts the latter at bit 29, so the peer association
command does not tell firmware that the peer supports 160 MHz.

Use the TLV definition for the 160 MHz peer flag. Other WMI interface
flag maps and the advertised VHT capabilities are unchanged.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/msm-modules/wlan-fw-api/+/c16fb8a901d149ab96b0ce6886845e3a82389d74/fw/wmi_unified.h#10201
Signed-off-by: Dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi-tlv.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi-tlv.h
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi-tlv.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/wmi-tlv.h
@@ -579,7 +579,7 @@
 	WMI_TLV_PEER_VHT = 0x02000000,
 	WMI_TLV_PEER_80MHZ = 0x04000000,
 	WMI_TLV_PEER_PMF = 0x08000000,
-	WMI_TLV_PEER_160MHZ = 0x20000000,
+	WMI_TLV_PEER_160MHZ = 0x40000000,
 };
 
 enum wmi_tlv_tag {
